      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Trailing and upright cultivars exist (NC State); this row stores the trailing reading. Hardy only in zones 10a to 11b (NC State), H2 (RHS), so it is bedding. Likes cool springs, struggles in hot humid summers. Watering: NC State consistently moist and drought intolerant; RHS reliably moist. Size: NC State 6 to 9 in tall and 6 to 12 in wide (its text says 4 to 9 in), RHS 10 to 50 cm. Toxicity: NC State rates humans medium severity (lobeline and lobelamine alkaloids; nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, drooling, weakness, dilated pupils, convulsions, coma after large amounts of any part) and does not mention cats or dogs; RHS says 'potentially harmful' without detail. No pet source was fetched, so the pet lines (graded 2) copy the human grading and symptoms and are the agent's mapping (from_knowledge_verify): review, and read the ASPCA page when one is found. The 'convulsions' sign is stored as tremor."
      },
